{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your oncology team members. I’ll be checking in on you during this admission. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m a bit tired, but okay. My neck still hurts, and I’ve been worried about starting the second round of chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You’re here for your second cycle of R-ICE chemotherapy, which we’re starting tomorrow. The good news is your last MRI showed the nasopharyngeal mass has shrunk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s good to hear. But why are we adding Rituxan this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your recent EBV viral load was elevated. Since you have CVID, your immune system can’t control EBV well, and it may be driving the lymphoma. Rituxan helps target those abnormal B cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, okay. That makes sense. Will it make me feel worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some patients feel a little flu-like during the first infusion, but we’ll give you pre-medications to help. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. My back’s been aching too—should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got an MRI of your lumbar spine today to check. It showed only your known degenerative changes from your prior surgery—no signs of lymphoma spreading there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was scared it might be cancer again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’re being extra cautious because of your history. Your spleen is a bit larger than before, but that’s common with lymphoma activity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my blood counts? Last time I was really low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is low at 1.5, and hemoglobin is 7.5, so we’ll keep an eye on it. We’ll transfuse if your hemoglobin drops below 7."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It helped me feel stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-03-19 14:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We also adjusted your diabetes meds. We’re using insulin now instead of your oral meds because steroids can raise blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-03-19 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I forgot I’m on dexamethasone with this chemo. My sugars have been high at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-03-19 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking your glucose four times a day and giving insulin as needed. Once you’re home, we’ll restart your glimepiride and metformin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-03-19 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my pain? I’m on methadone and dilaudid, but sometimes it’s not enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-03-19 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pain team reviewed your meds. We’re keeping your current doses. Pregabalin was increased last time and seems to be helping with nerve pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-03-19 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it has. My headaches are better too—probably from the chemo shrinking the mass?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-03-19 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s a good sign the treatment is working. We’ll keep monitoring with scans."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-03-20 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today we’ll start your R-ICE chemo, including Rituxan. It’ll take a few hours. Any questions before we begin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-03-20 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready. Will I lose my hair again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-03-20 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely, yes. But it will grow back after treatment ends. We can talk about scalp cooling if you’re interested."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-03-20 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Maybe later. I just want to get through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-03-20 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to support you. The nurse will start the infusion now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling today? Any nausea or fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little nauseated, but the ondansetron helps. No fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your white count is up to 2.0 today, which is improving. We’ll keep giving antibiotics to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still on acyclovir and atovaquone, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both continue. They help protect you from infections because of your CVID."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my IVIG? When’s my next dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get it in clinic in about two weeks. Your last level was good, so we’re keeping it every four weeks as you prefer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d rather not come more often. It’s a long trip."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-03-21 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We respect that. We’ll monitor your levels closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-03-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow you’ll get intrathecal methotrexate via lumbar puncture to protect your central nervous system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-03-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It was uncomfortable, but okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-03-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use fluoroscopy to guide the needle, and you’ll be awake but relaxed. We’ll collect some fluid to check for lymphoma cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-03-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-03-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll feel pressure, but we’ll numb the area first. Most patients tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-03-23 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The lumbar puncture went smoothly. We gave the methotrexate and sent the fluid for testing. No immediate issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-03-23 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I feel okay—just a little stiff."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-03-23 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ll keep you lying flat for a bit to reduce headache risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Already? That’s great. What about the Neupogen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get your first dose before you leave. You’ll inject it daily at home to help your white count recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve done it before. I’ll follow the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Continue all your usual meds, including methadone, clonazepam, and your inhaler."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your oncologist in a week, and your IVIG is scheduled in two weeks. Call us if you develop fever, severe pain, or confusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor. I feel like I’m on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Keep up the strength. We’re here for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—my hearing. It’s still not great since the ear surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. ENT said the tube is in place and the infection is cleared. The hearing loss may be from long-term inflammation, but they’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll follow up with them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and keep using the ofloxacin drops as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’m ready to go home and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge papers are ready. Your walker is here, and a nurse will go over your meds one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for everything. I really appreciate the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2156-03-23 12:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was our pleasure. Take care, and we’ll see you soon in clinic."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-03-19 14:39:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-03-23 14:35:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for her second cycle of R-ICE chemotherapy with added rituximab due to EBV viremia in the context of classical Hodgkin lymphoma and common variable immunodeficiency. She had ongoing neck pain and a history of intracranial involvement from lymphoma. Imaging showed response to prior treatment with decreased nasopharyngeal mass size. A lumbar MRI ruled out spinal involvement. She received intrathecal methotrexate for CNS prophylaxis and completed chemotherapy without complications. Her blood counts remained low but stable, requiring monitoring, and her diabetes was managed with insulin during the admission. She was discharged home with filgrastim to support white blood cell recovery and instructions to continue all home medications, including immunoprophylaxis and pain management.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Hodgkin's disease, nodular sclerosis, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Common variable immunodeficiency",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Anemia in neoplastic disease",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Colostomy status",
      "Hypotension, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Systemic sclerosis",
      "Exercise induced bronchospasm"
    ]
  }
}
